#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# phase_portrait

#% text
# `phase_portrait(L, q, t, [x, a, b], [v, c, d])` draws the streamlines of the motion of one coordinate `q` of the Lagrangian `L` in its phase plane: the position `x` from `a` to `b` across, the velocity `v` from `c` to `d` up.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The flow is `(x, v) -> (v, acc(x, v))` with the acceleration solved from the Euler-Lagrange equation; the parameters of `L` must have numeric values.

#% item
# Further arguments are options of `stream_plot`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The pendulum: libration inside the separatrix, rotation outside.

#% cell
phase_portrait(th'(t)^2/2 + cos(th(t)), th, t, [x, -4, 4], [v, -3, 3])
#% output
#= image("phase_portrait.files/phase_portrait-1.svgz")

#% text
# A damped double well, from a time-dependent Lagrangian:

#% cell
phase_portrait(exp(t/5)*(x'(t)^2/2 + x(t)^2/2 - x(t)^4/4), x, t, [x, -2, 2], [v, -2, 2])
#% output
#= image("phase_portrait.files/phase_portrait-2.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `stream_plot`, `n_dsolve_motion`, `equilibrium_points`
